---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How does Allfeat work?',
    a: 'Allfeat is a global decentralized registry that can be read and written by every player in the music industry — rights collectors, content creators, labels, publishers, distributors and tour managers alike.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why would a music entrepreneur use Allfeat?',
    a: 'In response to complex rights registration, tricky tracking processes and fragmented metadata, Allfeat offers a single collaborative registry anchored on the blockchain. It secures and certifies catalogs while timestamping the origin of musical creations.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the benefits for industry stakeholders?',
    a: 'Rights holders and master owners can make their metadata readable, enrich discovery and ownership data, and enable interoperability. Royalty collectors connect individuals (IPI, ISNI, IPN) and works (ISWC, ISRC, UPC) in a secure environment, so financial players can build new funding solutions for artists.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What tools are available?',
    a: 'ATS (Allfeat Time Stamp) is a white-label timestamping solution giving creators verifiable, tamper-proof proof of authorship. MIDDS (Music Industry Decentralized Data Structure) is a digital registry that secures and certifies catalogs with standardized metadata and an opt-out-by-default privacy architecture.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What technology protects the musical content?',
    a: 'Allfeat is powered by a purpose-built blockchain, developed over two years on Substrate and the Polkadot SDK in Rust. It uses a two-layer consensus model — Proof of Authority plus a social Proof of Metadata layer — backed by a strong DAO for protocol decisions.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why a dedicated blockchain for the music industry?',
    a: 'Allfeat is the first Layer-1 infrastructure designed specifically for music. General-purpose chains cannot always meet industry needs for performance, tailored functionality and cost efficiency — so Allfeat prioritizes security and large-scale data storage as the foundational layer of music’s digital ecosystem.',
  },
];
---

<section class="faq section" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq__grid">
    <div class="faq__head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--coral">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="display">Questions?</h2>
      <p class="body-muted faq__sub">
        Find the answers to your questions about Allfeat. Reach out if you need
        further insights.
      </p>
      <a href="#start" class="btn btn--ghost faq__contact">Contact the team</a>
    </div>

    <div class="faq__list reveal">
      {
        faqs.map((f, i) => (
          <div class={`faq-item card ${i === 0 ? 'is-open' : ''}`}>
            <button class="faq-q">
              <span>{f.q}</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-a">
              <p>{f.a}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .faq__head {
    position: sticky;
    top: 110px;
  }
  .faq__head .display {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .faq__sub {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .faq__contact {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .faq__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .faq-q {
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-warm-cream);
  }

  .faq-icon {
    position: relative;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .faq-icon::before,
  .faq-icon::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: var(--color-signal-teal);
    transition: transform 0.25s ease, opacity 0.25s ease;
  }
  .faq-icon::before {
    top: 7px; left: 0; width: 16px; height: 2px;
  }
  .faq-icon::after {
    left: 7px; top: 0; width: 2px; height: 16px;
  }
  .faq-item.is-open .faq-icon::after {
    transform: scaleY(0);
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .faq-a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows 0.3s ease;
  }
  .faq-item.is-open .faq-a {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }
  .faq-a > p {
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 0 24px;
    color: var(--color-mute-cream);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .faq-item.is-open .faq-a > p {
    padding-bottom: 22px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .faq__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }
    .faq__head {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
